{"title":"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the digits of a five-digit positive integer is 2. (A five-digit integer cannot start with zero.)\n</p><p>The number of such integers is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/588e1c179ca96c6e3923de0fc6f021779828b1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 1 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"388\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The only ways that a 5-digit number has digits adding up to two are either the number has a two and only 0's after or the number has two ones and three 0s.\n</p><p>There is only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> way to have a two and then only 0s after.\n</p><p>Next, if the number has 2 ones, one of them must be the first digit. This leaves 1 one and three 0s remaining, which can be arranged in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df4c17730df1c4ed5944f0889c781f87adc2389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{3! \\times 1!} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"90\" height=\"41\" /> different ways. We can also list all of the possible numbers and see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec8ae00a3a8801b6e34829593127dcca6247a10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd4f1de3b72b4a3cc0b1fb39a6103bb22d0537be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/882b5aa05a36b7ba80e31289644b35728cfe6360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10010$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de84c0b376e89ec3e59a710eff23de3350bec3c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c69708f2d970a96c515de8cbaf8bf1bc373a983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 4 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"121\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~hwd2022 and anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley\">1998 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a 